dsv41 patch 0071 (21.10.2026): background verify-depth cap by request priority. In use (VLLM_DSV41_BG_DEPTH=0, image
v19 and later): foreground decode +29 ... +56 % next to background requests; 0072 pauses their decode on top. Base:
the v12 files vllm/v1/core/sched/output.py, vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py and
vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/depth_policy.py (incl. our 0041/0043).
Why: our clients send a `priority` with each request (interactive 0, subagents 5, background jobs 10; vLLM runs with
--scheduling-policy priority, 0031c throttles background prefills). In our request log since 18.10. practically every
interactive request ran next to a background request. A second request in the step mostly adds the routed experts of
its rows: in the profile of 19.10. one request with 6 verify rows took 36.8 ms a round, two 60.2 ms, the MoE part
12.4 -> 30.8 ms. Background decodes still verified their full depth next to the foreground request.
How: NewRequestData carries the request's priority to the worker (output.py), the runner hands it to the depth policy
per slot (model_runner.py, add_requests), and while a decoding foreground request (priority < bgprio) is in the step,
every background request (priority >= bgprio) verifies at most "bg" drafts: under the conf rule its confidences past
bg are masked before the choice (a joint choice prices those rows as dead), and in every mode the chosen depth is
clamped after it. Its other window rows stay in the window as padding (no routed experts, as any row past a depth).
Device ops only, no host sync; both TP ranks see the same priorities and confidences, so they choose the same depths.
The depth only decides how many drafts can be accepted, never which tokens come out: outputs stay the same at T=0 and
keep their distribution at T > 0. Live switching through the depth file (rank 0 reads it and broadcasts it): "bg=<n>",
"bgprio=<p>". Tested on CPU: cap off = the original file's depths bit for bit (5 modes x 40 random cases); cap,
foreground detection, decoding mask, bgprio and the depth-file options checked.
Measured (21.10.2026, GB10, live on the production setup: image v19 with 0066/0067's MARKOV_FUSED and VOR_FUSED, GPU
2190 MHz; arms switched through the depth file, interleaved A/B/C/A/B/C, 2 runs per cell): one foreground request
(priority 0, 384 tokens, T=0) next to one or two background streams (priority 10, long outputs at T=0), foreground
decode tok/s with the cap off / bg=0 / bg=1:
  prose + 1 background stream    31.3 / 42.5 (+36 %) / 38.0 (+21 %)
  prose + 2 background streams   22.2 / 34.7 (+56 %) / 30.3 (+36 %)
  code + 1 background stream     50.9 / 65.7 (+29 %) / 61.3 (+20 %)
  code + 2 background streams    40.2 / 57.6 (+43 %) / 51.3 (+28 %)
First token 0.22-0.31 s in every arm. Capped at bg=0, a background stream gets one token a round, at more rounds per
second (one background stream: 15.7 -> 22.2 rounds with output per second during the foreground decode).
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_BG_DEPTH=<n> (default -1 = off), VLLM_DSV41_BG_MIN_PRIO=<p> (default 10: priority-5 requests count as
foreground); the depth-file tokens bg= / bgprio= override them live (bg=-1 = off). Needs priorities from the clients
and the depth policy (VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_POLICY, conf in the recipe launcher); without priorities nothing changes.

